sections=[
('A. Authority verification',f'Input HEAD `{head}` and branch match. The prior report, authority and every bound source/evidence hash verify unchanged. All 155 unrelated dirty entries are preserved. V3 and production files have zero task changes.'),
('B. Qualified baseline remesh','Generic discovery reproduces the sealed general-SDF vertex-depth map, coordinates, connectivity and hard-quality records exactly. The 536,679-pair certificate, complete volume audit and neighboring continuation remain bound by verified immutable authority. These expensive unchanged checks are reused, not described as freshly rerun.'),
('C. Study-case family','Four cases qualify: general-SDF branch-fold/overlap regression; a new closed narrowing channel with normalized planar SDF; two curved opposing spherical surfaces; and the analytic inward spherical cavity with a separate continuing control. These are new clean development supports, not the old SupportBlocked channel. No sealed geometry was changed. CASE_SUMMARY.json and each result.spec contain the definitions.'),
('D. Clean-support qualification','Each new case is scanned with the stored binary64 schedule. The complete pre-event stack receives all-cell quality, ownership, full unique-face exact certification and exact volume/degree validation. Channel and curved supports are clean through layer 3. The analytic support is clean through 12. A development control radius 0.04 at coarse resolution failed determinant; that unsealed control was rebuilt at radius 0.008 before qualification. The small analytic radius and layer-13 reference remain unchanged.'),
('E. Automatic cavity discovery','Actual failed cells, paired forbidden faces and dependent incidence seed the cavity. The first measured failure determines the first preceding-front proposal. Failed dependencies expand the active vertex set; continuing failure expands adjacency. Whole-fixture expansion is rejected and an earlier front is tried above protected layer 1. Full internal-face conflicts also feed back into discovery. No fixture ID, fixed ring count or universal rollback depth is used.'),
('F. Cavity expansion behavior','The first evidence-derived proposal succeeds for each measured case, including the baseline. Synthetic control-flow tests exercise lateral expansion, earlier-front fallback and ownership rejection. These tests are not presented as geometric qualification of arbitrary large cavities. Expansion records retain every evaluated proposal. A disconnected analytic control is handled without assuming graph connectivity to the event.'),
('G. Local layer-count maps','Baseline last-prism counts are 45 at 3, 145 at 4 and 1,346 at 5. Channel: 88 at 3 and 216 at 4. Curved: 32 at 3 and 224 at 4. Analytic: 32 at 12 and 32 at 13. Maps are derived from admitted cell connectivity. Their full arrays and measured adjacent differences are in accounting records. No universal difference-one rule is imposed; the reused templates support successive mixed cells over differing depths.'),
('H. Remeshing methods and reused tools','Reuse V4 variable-depth column reconstruction, node-alias prism termination, standard pyramid/tetrahedron templates, ownership, OpenFOAM-compatible quality, exact bilinear/planar intersections and exact oriented boundary-degree accounting. Gmsh 4.15.2 provides discrete-interface ingestion and one optional prescribed local tetrahedral fill. No custom general meshing kernel, optimizer or new dependency is needed. More complex remeshing tools were unnecessary for the qualified family.'),
('I. Mixed-cell topology','Pyramids and tetrahedra bridge terminated to surviving prisms in the channel, curved and general-SDF cases. Complete capping of the small analytic component needs no replacement transition cell. No wall face is remeshed and no first-layer coordinate changes. Unused upper coordinate slots are not mesh entities.\n\n| Case | Layers touched | Affected columns | Removed cells | New cell counts | Exact pairs |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---|---:|\n'+rows),
('J. Volume conformity','All admitted standard-cell maps are positive. Complete nonintersecting cell boundaries, opposite internal-face owners, closed oriented boundary, exact degree one at each cell interior, and exact cell/boundary volume equality jointly establish the repaired shell accounting. Degree samples alone are not a certificate. Each accounting record gives removed signed integral, replacement volume and preserved-volume relation. Invalid overlapping candidates do not define an additive occupied-volume sum. Receded exterior becomes future core space; it is not a gap inside the repaired shell. Zero overlaps and internal gaps remain.'),
('K. Hard-quality validation','All cells in each small fixture are checked, including preserved neighbors. Positive volume/exact cell validity, determinant >= 0.0011, interpolation weight >= 0.055, skewness <= 3.63636, symmetric volume ratio >= 0.01 and aspect <= 1000 pass where applicable. Existing prism, affine-tet and pyramid validity definitions remain unchanged. CASE_SUMMARY.json contains measured quality tails. No fake prism metrics, sigma/G thresholds or fixture exemptions were added.'),
('L. Continuous geometry','Complete unique-face exact checks include preserved–preserved, rebuilt–preserved and rebuilt–rebuilt interactions across the whole small fixture. All cases have zero forbidden and zero unresolved outcomes. The baseline eliminates all ten original cap/volume overlaps; new channel/curved event crossings are removed. No certificate mathematics changed.'),
('M. Outer interfaces','Each interface has exact matching incidence, opposite internal ownership, manifold vertex links, consistent orientation, no duplicate or zero-area faces and no exact self-intersection. Deterministic connectivity identities accompany the bound coordinate state. Multiple closed components are allowed and checked together. No unsupported hanging edges are introduced.'),
('N. Core-ingestion smoke','Gmsh ingests every interface with exact coordinate/connectivity round-trip; replay matches. The curved case also admits one prescribed tetrahedral cavity outside its interface, with fixed boundary, positive exact volume, exact interaction checks and zero interior degree relative to the shell. This optional smoke is geometric ingestion/fill evidence, not a general core-quality or CFD qualification. No global core was generated.'),
('O. Neighbor continuation','Each new case advances one surviving triangle column at the next stored nominal SDF target, creates a prism plus dependent transition cells, and passes complete fixture quality, volume and exact certification. The baseline reuses its bound column-1161 continuation. The analytic continuation lies on its separate larger component; the collapsed small component stays stopped. This is not a whole-shell next-layer qualification. A missing SDF-target check was found during audit: channel column 24 passed mesh gates but missed its target by 0.118468 mm. It is now rejected before admission; column 36 is fully verified after 32 rejected target assignments. The reproducer and regression test are retained.'),
('P. General-SDF regression','Qualified rollback remains layers 4–5: remove 45 prisms and two dependent tetrahedra; replace with 23 pyramids and 13 tetrahedra. Invalid cell 1232 stays absent. The exact old map is reproduced by the generic discovery path. Valid near-wall structure and distant cells remain identical.'),
('Q. Channel result','TerminationRemeshQualified on a new clean narrowing-channel support. Layer-4 quality/offset pinch and exact outer intersections initiate the bounded event. Eighty-eight columns are affected; 16 pyramids and 16 tetrahedra replace the rejected upper prisms. This qualifies the new clean channel, not the historical invalid support.'),
('R. Curved-case result','TerminationRemeshQualified. Opposing curved offset branches cross at layer 4 after a clean layer-3 support. Thirty-two columns are affected, with 16 pyramids and eight tetrahedra. The nonplanar outer interface, continuation and local outside-tet smoke pass.'),
('S. Analytic-capacity result','TerminationRemeshQualified. The preserved binary64 small-cavity radius yields its known geometric limit at 13. Its 32 columns stop at 12; the separate control remains layered at 13 and advances locally at 14. No near-zero spacing workaround or altered capacity witness is used. The exact layer schedule remains the nominal authority.'),
('T. Runtime and locality',f'Primary event timings exclude replay, clean-support setup and separately listed smoke. Full-fixture certification dominates this conservative bounded measurement. Surface remeshing and optimization cost are zero because existing templates suffice. Per-stage runtime files retain generation, quality, expansion, exact certification, accounting and RSS.\n\n| Case | Event seconds | Continuation seconds | Ingestion seconds |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n{cost}\n\nBaseline event cost is historical, not the cached current regression latency; its historical smoke was 22.282 s. Current family peak RSS is {peak:,} bytes. Largest changed column set is 88/304 (28.95%) in the small channel; the analytic component is 32/64 (50%) of its two-component fixture. No full-fixture remesh is performed. Replay and exploratory runs are excluded from production-like cost.'),
('U. Determinism','Independent execution matches cavity extent, map, removal manifest, coordinates, connectivity, quality, full exact results, volume accounting and continuation for all qualified cases. Supplemental accounting and Gmsh/tet replay match. Runtime and RSS are excluded from scientific identities.'),
('V. SF2 regression','Preserved Task-4L report and authority hashes verify unchanged. Zero termination/remesh regions, geometry changes, layer-count changes or correction changes. No production call site was added and no full SF2 run was made.'),
('W. Tests',tests['summary']+' Exact commands and results are in TESTS.json. Focused tests cover clean support, SDF target admission, seed dependencies, lateral/vertical expansion, ownership rejection, mixed reconstruction, volume and interface evidence, continuation, disconnected analytic components, baseline/SF2 preservation and exact replay. Existing relevant V4 tests are retained.'),
('X. Classification',classification+'. All four bounded cases qualify. This establishes small-family topology generalization, not arbitrary geometry or large-cavity performance. Expanded-boundary stress coverage and full core quality remain future work.'),
('Y. Production integration recommendation','Yes: bounded rollback/remeshing should be a production V4 capability under complete admission gates, wall/h1 protection, deterministic transactions and local scope. This recommendation does not deploy the study harness or a trigger policy. General initiation policy remains separate.'),
('Z. Recommended next task','A. Production termination/remesh trigger policy. The family now provides direct branch-fold/overlap, channel quality/pinch, curved collision and analytic-capacity initiation evidence. Keep topology acceptance independent of trigger decisions. That next task is not implemented here.')]
report='## Decision question\n\nDoes the bounded local rollback/remeshing architecture generalize across multiple clean termination geometries well enough to become a production V4 capability?\n\n'+'\n\n'.join('### '+title+'\n\n'+body for title,body in sections)+'\n'
